{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Breeze felt like a natural follow-up to Old Sock because I wanted more of that relaxed Clapton sound, and the JJ Cale connection made it my strongest choice.",
    "I Still Do and the blues-focused albums matched my interest in guitar-led music, so several suggestions felt relevant even though I only wanted one album."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Second Hand Heart leaned toward country when I was looking for blues and classic rock; enjoying Blown Away does not mean country is my priority today.",
    "I could not connect 25 or Very Best Of to my recent listening from those titles alone, so neither gave me enough reason to choose it."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Several suggestions treated an interest in blues as enough to make a live performance my next choice, but today I preferred a studio album.",
    "The country suggestion seemed to give too much weight to Blown Away compared with the blues and classic-rock connections that mattered more to this choice."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The specific connection to Old Sock mattered more than a broad resemblance: I wanted the relaxed Clapton and JJ Cale material offered by The Breeze.",
    "An album can fit my interests without making me want to choose it now. With only one pick today, the other blues albums did not displace my strongest match."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The suggestions understood my interest in blues and classic rock, but my immediate preference was a relaxed Clapton studio release."
}"}
